!! Single stylesheet

All CSS is defined in `styles.tid`, tagged `$:/tags/Stylesheet`. TiddlyWiki loads all stylesheet-tagged tiddlers at startup and injects them into the page. The `rr-` prefix namespaces all classes to avoid collisions with TW core or other plugins.

!! Reusable templates

Two wikitext templates provide parameterized UI components:

|!Template |!Tiddler |!Parameters |
|Callout |`$:/plugins/rimir/theme/callout` |`type` (info/warning/tip/danger), optional `label` |
|Notice |`$:/plugins/rimir/theme/notice` |`type` (warning/info/danger/success) |

These are consumed via `<$transclude $tiddler="..." type="...">` with `<$fill $name="body">` for content injection.

!! TW colour macros

The stylesheet uses TiddlyWiki's `<<colour ...>>` macros (e.g., `<<colour tiddler-border>>`, `<<colour page-background>>`, `<<colour muted-foreground>>`) to inherit the active palette's colors. This means rimir plugins automatically adapt to custom TW palettes.

!! Design principles

* ''Single source'' — one `styles.tid` file, no scattered CSS across plugins
* ''Prefix convention'' — all classes use `rr-` to avoid naming conflicts
* ''Palette-aware'' — uses TW colour macros, not hardcoded colors (except for semantic callout/notice borders)
* ''No JS'' — pure CSS + wikitext templates, no startup modules

